<# The grand report: every campaign of an experiment (see expkit/grand.py). #>
\documentclass[10pt]{article}
\usepackage[landscape,margin=1.4cm]{geometry}
\usepackage[table]{xcolor}
\usepackage{booktabs,longtable,graphicx,array,tikz}
\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{3.5pt}
\setlength{\parindent}{0pt}
<# One metric's colored tables: a block per combination of the facets, a row per campaign. #>
<% macro grid(s) %>
\begin{center}
<% for row in s.grid %>
<% for b in row %>
{\footnotesize\setlength{\tabcolsep}{2.2pt}\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.12}%
\begin{tabular}[t]{@{}l<% for _ in levels %>c<% endfor %>@{}}
\multicolumn{<< levels|length + 1 >>}{c}{\large\textbf{<< b.title|escape >>}}\\[0.3ex]
\texttt{<< col|escape >>} & <% for lv in levels %><< lv|level >><% if not loop.last %> & <% endif %><% endfor %>\\
\midrule
<% for r in b.rows %>
\hyperref[<< r.anchor >>]{<< r.campaign|escape >>} & <% for c in r.cells %><% if c.bg %>\cellcolor[HTML]{<< c.bg >>}<% endif %>\hyperlink{<< c.anchor >>}{\textcolor[HTML]{<< c.fg >>}{<% if c.bold %>\textbf{<< c.text >>}<% else %><< c.text >><% endif %><% if c.star %>$^*$<% endif %>}}<% if not loop.last %> & <% endif %><% endfor %>\\
<% endfor %>
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}}<% if not loop.last %>\hfill<% endif %>

<% endfor %>
\vspace{2ex}
<% endfor %>
\end{center}
<% endmacro %>
\begin{document}
\begin{center}
{\Large << cfg.experiment|escape >>: every campaign}\\[0.4ex]
{\small << built|escape >>}
\end{center}

<% if sections %>
<% set s = sections[0] %>
\section{<< s.label|escape >> at a glance}\label{sec:glance}
<% if col %>
Each block is one model; its columns run through \texttt{<< col|escape >>} (control << control|escape >>), its rows are the campaigns.
Cells are the seed mean of \texttt{<< s.metric|escape >>} (<< 'lower' if s.direction == 'min' else 'higher' >> is better), bold where best in its block's row, $^*$ where the paired difference against the control has $p < << alpha >>$.
The colour scale is per campaign, shared by all six blocks (spanning at least a tenth of the metric's range), so it compares models and levels within a task, not tasks.
Click a campaign for its <% if lengths %>length curves<% else %>figures<% endif %>, a cell for its loss curves.
<% endif %>
<< grid(s) >>

\clearpage
<% endif %>
\section{Status}
\autoref{tab:status} lists how much of every campaign's grid is stored.
<< n_results >> of << status|length >> campaigns have grid results.

{\small
\begin{longtable}{lrr}
\caption{Per campaign: grid runs stored/expected, and diverged.}\label{tab:status}\\
\toprule
campaign & runs & diverged\\
\midrule
\endhead
<% for r in status %>
<< r.campaign|escape >> & << r.stored >>/<< r.expected >> & << r.diverged >>\\
<% endfor %>
\bottomrule
\end{longtable}
}

<% if sections %>
\section{Per campaign}
<% if lengths %>
For each campaign, first \texttt{<< lengths.family|escape >>}$n$ against the input length $n$: a panel per model, a line per level of \texttt{<< col|escape >>} (seed means).
The shaded band is the training lengths and the red dashed line the longest of them: every length right of it is OOD.
<% if lengths.reference %>The point inside the band is \texttt{<< lengths.reference|escape >>}, pooled over the training lengths and drawn at their geometric mean.<% endif %>

<% endif %>
Then the loss curves of every cell: a row per model, a column per level of \texttt{<< col|escape >>}; seed mean of <% for n in loss_names %>\texttt{<< n|escape >>}<% if not loop.last %>, <% endif %><% endfor %>, shaded over the seed range; the dotted line is the median selected epoch.
<% for t in tasks %>
\clearpage
\subsection{<< t.campaign|escape >>}\label{sec:<< t.label >>}
<% if t.lengths %>
\begin{figure}[htbp]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\textwidth,height=0.82\textheight,keepaspectratio]{<< t.lengths >>}
\caption{<< t.campaign|escape >>: \texttt{<< lengths.family|escape >>}$n$ against input length $n$, per model and \texttt{<< col|escape >>}. Back to \hyperref[sec:glance]{the overview}.}
\label{<< t.label >>}
\end{figure}
<% else %>
\phantomsection\label{<< t.label >>}
<% endif %>
<% if t.loss %>
\begin{figure}[htbp]
\centering
\begin{tikzpicture}
\node[inner sep=0, anchor=south west] (img) {\includegraphics[width=\textwidth,height=0.86\textheight,keepaspectratio]{<< t.loss >>}};
\begin{scope}[x={(img.south east)}, y={(img.north west)}]
<% for a in t.anchors %>
\node[inner sep=0] at (<< '%.4f'|format(a.x) >>, << '%.4f'|format(a.y) >>) {\hypertarget{<< a.name >>}{}};
<% endfor %>
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{<< t.campaign|escape >>: loss curves per model (rows) and \texttt{<< col|escape >>} (columns). Back to \hyperref[sec:glance]{the overview}.}
\end{figure}
<% endif %>
<% endfor %>

<% if sections|length > 1 %>
\clearpage
\appendix
\section{Other metrics}
The same blocks for every other metric; the full tables, with confidence intervals and differences against the control, are the \texttt{grand\_<metric>.csv} files next to this report.
<% for s in sections[1:] %>
\clearpage
\subsection{<< s.label|escape >> (\texttt{<< s.metric|escape >>}, << 'lower' if s.direction == 'min' else 'higher' >> is better)}
<< grid(s) >>
<% endfor %>
<% endif %>
<% else %>
\section{Results}
No campaign has grid results yet: run \texttt{scripts/run\_all.sh}.
<% endif %>
\end{document}
